proto_socks: Log IP-only SOCKS requests at info, not warn

Tor warns, at most once every 5 seconds per process, whenever a SOCKS
client gives it an IP address instead of a host name, since the client
may have leaked the name through its own DNS lookup.  The option that
silenced this, WarnUnsafeSocks, is obsolete and ignored.  Behind
gwtor's gwproxy such clients are expected and known, and the warning
only floods the logs.  Log it at info level instead; the controller
event and SafeSocks behave as before.

diff --git a/src/core/proto/proto_socks.c b/src/core/proto/proto_socks.c
index 08c1793456f3..0c76773a300f 100644
--- a/src/core/proto/proto_socks.c
+++ b/src/core/proto/proto_socks.c
@@ -65,7 +65,12 @@ log_unsafe_socks_warning(int socks_protocol, const char *address,
   /* note the subtle "||" here: either warn every time, or else
    * warn in a rate-limited way otherwise. */
   if (warn_every_time || (m = rate_limit_log(&socks_ratelim, approx_time()))) {
-    log_warn(LD_APP,
+    /* gwtor: info, not warn.  Clients behind gwtor's gwproxy may resolve
+     * names themselves, knowingly; at warn level this message floods the
+     * logs (once every 5 seconds per Tor process) with nothing to act on.
+     * The controller event below is still sent, and SafeSocks still
+     * rejects such requests when it is set. */
+    log_info(LD_APP,
              "Your application (using socks%d to port %d) is giving "
              "Tor only an IP address. Applications that do DNS resolves "
              "themselves may leak information. Consider using Socks4A "
